{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The combined model’s task scorers still use only the target and individual history events; they cannot use the feedback memory that feeds the shared representation. I’ll test a small connection from that memory into the scorers, with a matched static-input control and private versus averaged task routing.\n\nThe current gain over the stronger source is 0.000697 macro AUC and costs about 20% more wall time, with a small click-AUC regression. The proposal will preserve those trade-offs and reserve budget for attribution and paired repetitions.\n"}}
